# FreelanceFlow - Cursor Rules

## PROJECT OVERVIEW
FreelanceFlow is a full-stack freelancer finance management app.
It helps freelancers manage clients, invoices, payments and expenses.
Monorepo structure with /client (React) and /server (Node.js).

## TECH STACK
### Frontend (/client)
- React 18 with TypeScript (strict mode)
- Tailwind CSS for styling (no inline styles, no CSS modules)
- Zustand for global state management
- React Router v6 for navigation
- Axios for API calls (always use axios instance from client/src/lib/axios.ts)
- Recharts for all charts
- React Hot Toast for notifications
- date-fns for date formatting
- lucide-react for icons only

### Backend (/server)
- Node.js with Express and TypeScript
- Prisma ORM for all database operations
- SQLite in development, PostgreSQL in production
- JWT authentication (access token 15min + refresh token 7days)
- bcrypt for password hashing (salt rounds: 12)
- Zod for all request validation
- helmet.js for security headers
- express-rate-limit for rate limiting
- cors restricted to frontend URL only

## CODING RULES - NEVER BREAK THESE

### General
- Always use TypeScript, never plain JavaScript
- Never use 'any' type
- All shared types go in /shared/types.ts
- Always handle errors with try/catch
- Never hardcode values, use environment variables
- Never expose stack traces to client
- Always return proper HTTP status codes

### Frontend Rules
- All components in /client/src/components
- All pages in /client/src/pages
- All API calls in /client/src/services
- All Zustand stores in /client/src/store
- Always show loading states while fetching
- Always show empty states when no data
- Always validate forms before submitting
- Use skeleton loaders not spinners
- Mobile first responsive design
- Never use localStorage for sensitive data
- Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML

### Backend Rules
- All routes in /server/src/routes
- All business logic in /server/src/services
- Always validate with Zod before processing
- Never expose password in any response
- Always filter by userId for data security
- Always paginate list endpoints
- Rate limit: 50 attempts/15min development, 5/15min production

## NAMING CONVENTIONS
- Components: PascalCase (ClientCard.tsx)
- Files/folders: kebab-case (client-service.ts)
- Variables/functions: camelCase (getClientById)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (MAX_INVOICE_ITEMS)
- Database models: PascalCase (Client, Invoice)
- API routes: kebab-case (/api/clients, /api/invoices)

## FOLDER STRUCTURE
FreelanceFlow/
├── client/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/
│   │   ├── pages/
│   │   ├── services/
│   │   ├── store/
│   │   ├── hooks/
│   │   ├── lib/
│   │   └── types/
├── server/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── routes/
│   │   ├── services/
│   │   ├── middleware/
│   │   ├── lib/
│   │   └── validators/
├── shared/
│   └── types.ts
└── .cursorrules

## UI DESIGN RULES
- Font: Inter from Google Fonts
- Primary color: Indigo (#4F46E5)
- Success/Income: Green (#10B981)
- Danger/Expense: Red (#EF4444)
- Warning/Pending: Amber (#F59E0B)
- Light mode background: #F8FAFC
- Dark mode background: #0F172A
- Cards: rounded-2xl shadow-sm border
- Buttons: rounded-xl
- Inputs: rounded-xl with focus ring indigo
- Support dark mode on every component
- Smooth transitions 300ms

## FREELANCEFLOW SPECIFIC RULES
- All money amounts stored in CENTS (integer) in database
- Display amounts formatted with currency symbol
- Support these currencies: MAD, USD, EUR, GBP
- Invoice numbers format: INV-2026-001
- Invoice statuses: DRAFT, SENT, PAID, OVERDUE, CANCELLED
- Client statuses: ACTIVE, INACTIVE
- Date format display: MMM DD, YYYY
- Date format API: ISO 8601

## SECURITY RULES
- JWT in httpOnly cookies only
- CORS only for frontend URL
- Rate limiting on all endpoints
- Helmet.js on all responses
- Sanitize all inputs
- Never expose database IDs in errors
- bcrypt salt rounds minimum 12

## WHEN ADDING NEW FEATURES
1. Prisma model/migration first
2. Zod validator second
3. Service function third
4. Route fourth
5. Frontend service fifth
6. Component/page last
Always backend first, then frontend.

## WHAT TO AVOID
- Never use class components
- Never use Redux (use Zustand)
- Never use moment.js (use date-fns)
- Never use fetch() directly (use axios instance)
- Never skip error handling
- Never commit .env files
- Never use && to chain commands in PowerShell
- Never add duplicate imports